From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:02:14 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: add the ADSP voice services

The ADSP exposes MVM, CVS and CVP -- the multimode voice manager, the
core voice stream and the voice processor -- on APR services 9, 10 and
11. Without nodes for them the APR bus never instantiates the devices,
so no driver can reach the services at all: apr_send_pkt() takes the
destination service from the apr_device it is called on, and there is no
back door.

The nodes are inert on their own. They cost three device registrations
and share the audio protection domain already used by the other four
services.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index 893cb6a4be87..2697f471db5c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -4634,6 +4634,24 @@ q6routing: routing {
 							#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 						};
 					};
+
+					q6mvm: service@9 {
+						reg = <APR_SVC_ADSP_MVM>;
+						qcom,protection-domain = "avs/audio",
+									 "msm/adsp/audio_pd";
+					};
+
+					q6cvs: service@a {
+						reg = <APR_SVC_ADSP_CVS>;
+						qcom,protection-domain = "avs/audio",
+									 "msm/adsp/audio_pd";
+					};
+
+					q6cvp: service@b {
+						reg = <APR_SVC_ADSP_CVP>;
+						qcom,protection-domain = "avs/audio",
+									 "msm/adsp/audio_pd";
+					};
 				};
 			};
 		};
